  "surprise": "P37 / P34 x P32 layer-wise hybrid (blocks 0/2/4 all-ALiBi with 115's slopes 1/4..1/256 each on two heads, blocks 1/3/5 all-NoPE; same 48-slot slope multiset as 115, 4,800,000 params; cached vs full forward max logit diff 8.9e-7 on CPU) scored 602/647/541 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 115-fable's 639/646/609: exact means 596.67 vs 631.33, -34.67, paired -37/+1/-68, inside the registered -45..+35 range but near its bottom (central -5). Discard. Pretraining was unchanged as predicted: 4250/4233/4206 steps (115: 4204/4218/4263), final val loss 0.0803/0.0824/0.0819, held-out greedy 0.984/0.985/0.976. The registered mechanism is REFUTED at the RL start: round-1 targets solved 579/315/262 vs 718/756/691 and round-1 parse failures 43/50/54% of 48,000 samples vs 115's 25/22/18%, i.e. back in all-ALiBi 113's territory (50/30/64%). So whole all-ALiBi layers over-localise at 7+ lines as much as ALiBi everywhere, even with an all-NoPE layer after each one: what made 115 well-formed at unseen lengths is the per-block pairing of NoPE and ALiBi heads, not the head-slot budget. Surprise: RL recovered most of the gap (r1->r4 +505/+805/+732, r4 targets 1084/1120/994 vs 115's 1131/1122/1065), and seed 1 matched 115 (647 vs 646) from a 315-target start; eval ge10 92/102/73 vs 103/97/89. Seed 1 ran on a slow-CPU pod (Lean gate 112/257/347 s wall and up to 30,397 CPU-s per 48k pass vs 55-110 s and <=8,718 CPU-s on seeds 0/2; 108-139 samples/s) and finished at 2258 s of 2400: pod, not model.",
